      "content": "but that feels so naive though. like reading a book where you already know the ending. you can pretend you're an author, but the biology is the real script. my family... they didn't just struggle, they ended up completely destroyed by it. if the end is already decided, isn't fighting it just making the middle part more painful? it feels like i'm just delaying the inevitable and making myself suffer more in the process.",
